(3) "Qualifying payroll" means the amount of compensation used to determine the withholding obligations in division (A) of section 5747.06 of the Revised Code and paid over one of the following periods by the entity whose sale generated the qualifying capital gain:

(a) The five calendar years immediately preceding the time of sale for a taxpayer described in division (A)(1)(a)(i) of this section;

(b) The investment period, not to exceed the five calendar years, immediately preceding the time of sale for a taxpayer described in division (A)(1)(a)(ii) of this section.
